<LegalLayout
	title="Terms of Service"
	description="Vezne Terms of Service — the terms that govern use of the Vezne personal finance app."
	lastUpdated="24 July 2026"
>
	<section>
		<h2>1. Acceptance of these Terms</h2>
		<p>
			These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of
			Vezne (the "Service"), a personal finance tracking application. By
			creating an account or otherwise using the Service, you agree to
			be bound by these Terms and by our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
			If you do not agree, do not use the Service.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>2. What Vezne is — and isn't</h2>
		<p>
			Vezne helps you record, categorize, and review your own income and
			expenses, including importing bank statement files you upload
			yourself. Vezne is <strong>not</strong> a bank, a licensed
			financial institution, an investment adviser, or a payment
			service provider. It does not connect to your bank accounts, move
			money, or provide financial, tax, or legal advice. Nothing in the
			Service should be treated as such advice.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>3. Your account</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				You must provide a valid email address and keep your password
				confidential; you're responsible for activity under your
				account.
			</li>
			<li>
				You may sign in with a password or with Google Sign-In, at your
				choice.
			</li>
			<li>
				You can delete your account at any time from Settings. Deletion
				deactivates the account immediately with a 30-day window to
				restore it by signing back in; after that window, the account's
				data is permanently deleted. See the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
				for details.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
		<p>You agree not to:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Use the Service for any unlawful purpose.</li>
			<li>
				Attempt to access another user's data, probe or bypass the
				Service's access controls, or interfere with its normal
				operation.
			</li>
			<li>
				Upload files you don't have the right to upload, or content that
